    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "017dcf87cfea7d856186a69e85853a23322c631f8b1f37effb1a3c84ab7e3d98",
      "text": "After breakfast, travel north into Imbabura Province. The drive to Otavalo takes around two hours, while the full sightseeing day lasts approximately eight hours.\n\nEn route, stop at Calderón and Guayllabamba to see traditional dough figurines and sample local produce, including cherimoya. Continue via Miralago, where a local family offers a tasting of bizcochos and fresh layered cheese. At a scenic viewpoint, take in Imbabura Volcano and San Pablo Lake.\n\nAround midday, arrive at Otavalo's famous Plaza de los Ponchos, a major Indigenous craft market selling textiles, clothing, jewellery and handmade goods. Enjoy time to browse the stalls, see local crafts and experience northern Ecuador beyond the principal tourist attractions.\n\nContinue to Cotacachi, known for its leather goods, and then visit Peguche Waterfall, reached by a short path through eucalyptus woodland. The waterfall has special cultural importance to local Indigenous communities.\n\nEnd the day at historic Hacienda Pinsaqui and check in at Pinsaqui 4★. Meals: breakfast.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-chat-3of5-20261105-0150-B",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The approved Word day 7 covers Otavalo, Calderón, Guayllabamba, San Pablo Lake and Peguche, but omits the Miralago tasting, Cotacachi leather stop, eucalyptus trail, eight-hour timing and extended pinned RU narrative; translate these sections from RU."
      }
    },
